      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "coag_s1_lev1_so4",
          "description": "First step, surface layer: the initial, nearly unimodal Aitken/accumulation distribution. Reference: the em_scm_xy chem_opt = 170 column (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, reference namelist unchanged), MOSAIC coagulation capture dumps/chem170_mosaic_coag (WRF fork earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 f311091e; bit-identical to dumps/chem170_wrf on every shared field), model step 1, column level 1. Inputs are coagsolv's own entry state: dry diameters coag_dpdry and the distribution coag_distrib (number in #/cm3; the composition quantity here is column 1 of 13, so4, in mol/mol-air). The kernel cbr and every expected value come from the REAL64 replay of coagsolv on those inputs (kernels/coagsolv_rate_driver, chem170_scm/coag64/r64_1.json), because WRF's real32 coagsolv forms the small high-side split shares as 1 - finklow and keeps only a few digits of them (FORTRAN_BUGS N117); the real32 replay of the same inputs agrees with the in-model rates to real32 round-off. Tolerances measured over all 16 steps x 59 levels, not assumed: splitting tables 4.4e-16 absolute (bound 1e-12), number rates 1.6e-10 relative per bin (bound 1e-9), composition rates 1.9e-10 of the column's largest bin rate (bound 1e-9 relative with an absolute floor of 1e-9 of that maximum, because production and loss cancel to 1.4e-8 relative in the smallest entries).",
